<title>GERMANY: German state of Bavaria details April CPI data.</title>
<headline>German state of Bavaria details April CPI data.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The statistics Office in the west German state of Bavaria said on Thursday that the cost of living fell at -0.2 percent in April from March but rose 1.1 percent from the same month one year ago.</p>
<p>						 Percentage change</p>
<p> Index/component			   mth/mth   yr/yr    Index</p>
<p> Overall price index		     -0.2	+1.1     115.1</p>
<p> Prices exc services and repairs     +0.1	+1.4     122.3</p>
<p> Rents					 +0.2	+2.8     128.8</p>
<p> Household energy			  +0.2	+2.7     123.9</p>
<p> Personal goods, services and other  -3.5	+1.0     120.2</p>
<p> Transport and communications	  -0.1	-0.2     115.4</p>
<p> Furniture and other household goods +0.3	+0.5     110.1</p>
<p> Foodstuffs, drinks, tobacco	   +0.3	+0.5     109.7</p>
<p> Clothing, shoes			   +0.1	+0.9     107.4</p>
<p> Health and personal care items	+0.1	+1.1     115.0</p>
<p> Education, entertainment, leisure   -0.1	+1.7     111.5</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
